<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41101" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ -nāvĭgo</span></b> ,
			āvi, 1, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i>, <i>to sail back.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">post in haec Puteolana et Cumana regna
					renavigaro,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 14, 16, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ab Asturā Antium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					32, 1, 1, § 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex Indiā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 6,
					23, 26, § 106</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Acheron invius Renavigari,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Fur. 716</span></i>
			.</div>
